# {{name}}

A GPUI-CE counter app with Subsecond hot-patching enabled.

Requires Rust 1.95 or newer, `gpui`, and the native dependencies from
[GPUI-CE's setup guide](https://github.com/gpui-ce/gpui-ce/blob/main/SETUP.md).
macOS requires Xcode, including its Metal compiler. Linux requires a working
Wayland or X11 display.

```sh
gpui watch
```

Click **Increment**, then edit the background or label in `src/main.rs` and
save. Render changes should appear while preserving the counter.

Restart watch after changing state layouts or function signatures. Hot patching
is experimental. Dependencies are pinned to a compatible GPUI-CE revision;
update both `rev` values together when upgrading, and check that its Subsecond
version is supported by your CLI.

The app is a standalone Cargo workspace. To join an existing workspace, remove
its `[workspace]` section and add the app to the parent workspace's members.

